Here is a complete step-by-step implementation to create a data table with expandable rows in Salesforce LWC, where the expanded content dynamically loads record details from Apex.

We will:

1. Create an Apex class to fetch record data.


2. Build a child LWC (generalInformation) that receives a recordId and calls the Apex method.


3. Build a parent LWC (dataTableWithDropdown) to show the table and toggle the dropdown.




---

🧩 Step-by-Step Implementation


---

✅ Step 1: Apex Controller to Fetch Record

Create the following Apex class in Salesforce:

public with sharing class GeneralInfoController {
    @AuraEnabled(cacheable=true)
    public static Account getRecordInfo(Id recordId) {
        return [SELECT Id, Name, Phone, Website FROM Account WHERE Id = :recordId LIMIT 1];
    }
}

> 🔄 You can change Account to any object (like Lead, Opportunity, etc.)




